<title>MALAYSIA: Petronas say to set up petrol pumps in Philippines.</title>
<headline>Petronas say to set up petrol pumps in Philippines.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia national oil firm Petronas's said on Tuesday it plans to expand its retail network in Southeast Asia to include the Philippines.</p>
<p>&quot;We have planned to set up retail in Mindanao in the Philippines,&quot; president and chief excutive officer Hassan Marican told Reuters on the sidelines of an oil and gas conference.</p>
<p>When asked the timing of the company's plans, Marican said &quot;it'll depend on market conditions.&quot;</p>
<p>Petronas currently runs 12 service stations in Phnom Penh in Cambodia and two in Bangkok in Thailand.  </p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur Newsroom (+603 230 6894)</p>
